  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="f202-cafd-dd2d-1afe" name="Kiavahran Repulsor Field" hidden="false">
      <description>All Shrouded Damage Mitigation rolls made by a unit with this Special Rule have their result improved by 1, granting the unit the Shrouded (6+) Special Rule if it does not already have it. Additionally, when targeted by an enemy unit during the Interceptor Reaction, the enemy unit must pass an Initiative test. If this succeeds, proceed as normal. If it fails, the enemy unit's Ballistic Skill is reduced by 1 for the duration of the Interceptor attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="28fd-1a7a-de38-2267" name="Raptor Lieutenant" hidden="false">
      <description>Navar Hef may only join units of Raptors, Proto-Astartes or Raptors, Mutated.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e6a4-fcae-17b5-097c" name="Warlord: No Witnesses" hidden="false">
      <description>If chosen as the army's Warlord, Navar Hef automatically has No Witnesses as his Warlord Trait and may not select any other Warlord Trait.
Navar Hef and any model in a unit he is part of that has the Legiones Astartes (Raven Guard) special rule gain +1 to their Weapon Skill Characteristic on any turn in which they make a successful charge which is not Disordered.
In addition, an army with Navar Hef as its Warlord may make an additional Reaction during their opponent's Assault phase as long as Navar Hef has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b814-23b7-a6b0-22cd" name="Warlord: Vital Strike" hidden="false">
      <description>If chosen as the army's Warlord, Nykona Sharrowkyn automatically has Vital Strike as his Warlord Trait and may not select any other Warlord Trait.
When rolling to wound with any weapon with the Rending, Breaching or Murderous Strike Special Rules, Nykona Sharrowkyn and any unit entirely composed of models with the Legiones Astartes (Raven Guard) he has joined treat those rules as being one point lower than the profile on their weapon - for example, a weapon with Breaching (4+) would be counted as Breaching (3+).
In addition, an army with Nykona Sharrowkyn as its Warlord may make an additional Reaction during their opponent's Assault phase as long as Nykona Sharrowkyn has not been removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
